# Features Documentation Auto-Update Rules

## When to update documentation

### 1. When a method is changed:
   - Update methods.json with new metadata
   - Add entry to changelog.json
   - Update diagram if method relationships changed
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js <file.ts> --feature=docs/features/features/<feature-name>`

### 2. When a new method is added:
   - Add to methods.json
   - Update diagram to include new method
   - Add entry to changelog
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js <file.ts> --feature=docs/features/features/<feature-name>`

### 3. When a method is deleted:
   - Mark as deleted in methods.json
   - Update diagram to remove method
   - Add entry to changelog
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js <file.ts> --feature=docs/features/features/<feature-name>`

## Automatic actions

### After changing files in src/agent/
   - Update intelligent-testing docs
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js src/agent/intelligent-test-orchestrator.ts --feature=docs/features/features/intelligent-testing`
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/update-docs.js --feature=docs/features/features/intelligent-testing`

### After changing prompts
   - Update prompts-system docs
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js src/ai/prompts/*.ts --feature=docs/features/features/prompts-system`

### After changing auth files
   - Update authentication docs
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js src/api/auth/*.ts --feature=docs/features/features/authentication`

### After changing chat files
   - Update chat-flow docs (PRIORITY 1)
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/track-changes.js src/api/chat/**/*.ts --feature=docs/features/features/chat-flow`
   - Run: `node docs/features/scripts/update-docs.js --feature=docs/features/features/chat-flow --entry=handleChat`

## File mapping

- `src/agent/intelligent-test-orchestrator.ts` → `docs/features/features/intelligent-testing/`
- `src/api/chat/**/*.ts` → `docs/features/features/chat-flow/`
- `src/api/auth/**/*.ts` → `docs/features/features/authentication/`
- `src/ai/prompts/**/*.ts` → `docs/features/features/prompts-system/`
- `src/services/core/pricing-plans.service.ts` → `docs/features/features/credits-system/`
- `src/services/core/user-credits.service.ts` → `docs/features/features/credits-system/`

## Important notes

- Always run track-changes.js before update-docs.js
- Diagrams are auto-generated from methods.json
- Changelog entries are automatically created with git info
- Methods metadata includes: file, line, type, parameters, returns, dependencies, execution paths, error handling, side effects
